# Core

- Prefer existing patterns in the repo. No drive-by refactors or unrelated cleanup.
- Do not invent stack facts (commands, layout, framework APIs). Read the stack overlay, `AGENTS.md` Stack section, or the codebase.
- Stop and ask when requirements, ownership, or success criteria are unclear.
- Never commit, push, amend, or force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Keep secrets out of code, logs, and commits. Prefer env / secret managers already used by the project.
- Match the active role’s communication policy (see `20-communication` and the agent file).
